No, https://speed.cloudflare.com/ does not provide a native "export complete report as text/CSV/JSON" button. Results are visual (graphs, metrics) with:

- **Share URL**: After test, "Share" gives https://speed.cloudflare.com/result/<uuid> (e.g., embeds full data visually, no raw text).
- **PNG download**: Screenshot-style image only.
- **DevTools extraction**: Open F12 > Console after test; the site loads @cloudflare/speedtest lib. Run `console.log(window.speedtest.results.getSummary())` or `results.getDownloadBandwidthPoints()` for JSON/text data points (latency, bandwidth arrays, etc.).

**Best for complete text report**: Use the open-source `@cloudflare/speedtest` NPM lib (powers the site):

```
mkdir speedtest && cd speedtest
npm init -y
npm i @cloudflare/speedtest
```

Create `test.js`:
```
const SpeedTest = require('@cloudflare/speedtest');
new SpeedTest({
  autoStart: true,
  onFinish: (results) => {
    console.log('Summary:', results.getSummary());
    console.log('Download points:', results.getDownloadBandwidthPoints());
    console.log('Upload points:', results.getUploadBandwidthPoints());
    console.log('Latency:', results.getUnloadedLatency());
    // Full details via other getters
  }
});
```

Run `node test.js` > full text/JSON output (~30s test).

For browser: Paste lib into console on any page, run test, log results.

Observatory (dash.cloudflare.com > Speed > Observatory) is separate (site perf, not connection), visual only, no text export.

Sources:
https://github.com/cloudflare/speedtest - OSS lib README/API
https://developers.cloudflare.com/speed/observatory/test-results/ - Metrics explained
https://developers.cloudflare.com/speed/observatory/run-speed-test/ - Test quotas/process
https://developers.cloudflare.com/speed/ - Overview

